```js
function inviteAdmin(request) {
  if (!request.user) throw new Error('Unauthenticated');
  if (request.user.role !== 'owner') throw new Error('Forbidden');
  // optional: verify request.user.accountId === request.body.accountId
  addAdmin(request.body.identifier, request.body.accountId);
  return { success: true };
}
```
This ensures the server enforces both authentication and authorization, preventing lower‑privileged users from executing Owner‑only functions.

Add server‑side verification before any business logic runs. Example PHP fix:
<?php
    $token = $_POST['g-recaptcha-response'] ?? '';
